# Copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit the real .env file.

# Talk mode in the hum feature (hum/engine/talk). Without them the song still gets made; only the
# chat/voice edits say "GEMINI_API_KEY is missing".
GEMINI_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Optional
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb

# Optional: where hummed recordings and songs are kept (default backend/hum_data, never served by URL)
# HUM_DATA_DIR=
# Optional: a General MIDI soundfont for rendering songs. Default: the copy in
# hum/engine/accompanist/soundfonts/ (see hum/README.md)
# SOUNDFONT_PATH=

# ---- Production (Cloud Run) ----
# Production mode turns on by itself when DJANGO_ENV=production or K_SERVICE is set (Cloud Run sets
# K_SERVICE in every container). Locally none of this is needed. In production the server REFUSES TO
# START unless these three are set (server/config.py):
# DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=        # a long random string, not the development default
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=            # the server's host names, comma separated, e.g. my-service-abc.a.run.app (no '*')
# APP_API_KEY=              # the shared key the app sends in the X-App-Key header
# Optional: requests per client per minute. Production defaults: 30 for /api/hum/*, 120 for the rest.
# 0 turns a limit off, and locally both are off unless you set them.
# RATE_LIMIT_HUM_PER_MINUTE=
# RATE_LIMIT_DEFAULT_PER_MINUTE=

# ---- Where score MusicXML is read from ----
# Local disk (backend/storage/musicxml, filled by `manage.py import_pdmx`) is used first. If a file isn't there
# and this is set, it is fetched from this address, e.g. a Cloudflare R2 bucket's public URL. Production sets it.
# MUSICXML_BASE_URL=https://pub-xxxx.r2.dev
# Hum working files older than this many hours are deleted, checked every HUM_SWEEP_MINUTES (container only).
# HUM_TTL_HOURS=3
# HUM_SWEEP_MINUTES=10

# ---- The public Privacy Policy, Terms and Support pages (/privacy, /terms, /support) ----
# The text is in backend/legal/ and is filled in from these. They need no key, so App Review can read them.
# Production REFUSES TO START unless SUPPORT_EMAIL is a real address, because it is printed on the policy:
# SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@yourdomain.com
# Who the policy and terms call "we" (default AG):
# LEGAL_PUBLISHER=AG
# HUM_TTL_HOURS above is also the retention the policy states, so changing it changes the policy text.
